  "worked_solution": "Let's plot the graph of $y=cos\u2061x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933487/assets/88378ece5b1721cdc533d07d69c004901539c7f8fda9a5a3e5c5648ed32905c5.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. The function has a maximum at $x=0,\\pm 2\\pi ,\u2026,$ which can be written as $x=2n\\pi .$\n\n- Statement II is true. At $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$, the function intersects the $x$-axis.\n\n- Statement III is false. The minimum value is $-1$, the maximum value is $1$, and so the range is $[-1,1].$",
